#!/bin/sh
# deinstall.oosh - RETIRED 2026-10-07.
# Reason: nothing in oosh deletes without asking - owner decision 2026-10-07.
# It used to remove /home/shared, ~/oosh, ~/config and the user developking without a question.

cat >&2 <<'MSG'
init/deinstall.oosh is retired: it no longer deletes anything.
Nothing in oosh deletes without asking - owner decision 2026-10-07.

For your own oosh use:  oo deinstall
  (asks for confirmation and keeps backups as .orig.<ts>)

Removing the shared tree, sharedConfig and the user developking is a manual,
deliberate action. For information only, the old script removed:
  /home/shared        (shared tree and sharedConfig)
  /home/developking   (home of the user developking; the user itself via: user delete.linux developking)
  ~/oosh  ~/config  ~/init  ~/config.initial  ~/.once
MSG
exit 1
